\newlabel{RF2}{12}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The 552 annotated Yellowfin images are divided into training (441) and test (111) subsets. Segmentation masks are generated with SAM2 under tuned hyperparameters, and mask candidates are further partitioned into training, validation, and held-out sets. After bootstrapping and augmentation ($\phi (\cdot )$), each CNN submodel is trained independently on cropped mask regions, producing class-probability outputs from the function, $\hat  {f}^{(m)}(\cdot )$. These outputs are aggregated into an $N \times M \times K$ matrix of ensemble probabilities, from which the ensemble optimizer learns calibrated weights to combine submodels. Final performance is assessed out-of-sample, first on mask discrimination ability of the \emph  {ensemble model} itself and then on the full machine vision pipeline (see Figure~\ref {fig:pipeline}), which integrates mask classification with segmentation to produce live coral cover estimates.}}{12}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:training_pipeline}{{5}{12}{The 552 annotated Yellowfin images are divided into training (441) and test (111) subsets. Segmentation masks are generated with SAM2 under tuned hyperparameters, and mask candidates are further partitioned into training, validation, and held-out sets. After bootstrapping and augmentation ($\phi (\cdot )$), each CNN submodel is trained independently on cropped mask regions, producing class-probability outputs from the function, $\hat {f}^{(m)}(\cdot )$. These outputs are aggregated into an $N \times M \times K$ matrix of ensemble probabilities, from which the ensemble optimizer learns calibrated weights to combine submodels. Final performance is assessed out-of-sample, first on mask discrimination ability of the \emph {ensemble model} itself and then on the full machine vision pipeline (see Figure~\ref {fig:pipeline}), which integrates mask classification with segmentation to produce live coral cover estimates}{figure.caption.7}{}}
