\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B.15}{\ignorespaces Pixel-level segmentation accuracy versus water depth for training (teal) and held-out test (salmon) images. The x-axis follows Yellowfin's native sign convention for depth below the water surface (more negative = deeper; 0 = surface). \emph  {Left:} full range of observed depths and accuracies. \emph  {Right:} subset containing 92.0\% of all images (0--7.5\,m depth, 75--100\% accuracy) with a nearly flat linear trend. Across the sampled depths, accuracy remains high with no systematic degradation.}}{34}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
